course: dictionary
lesson: 4870
title: Iconic: famous and easy to recognise
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The Eiffel Tower is an iconic building.» Iconic describes the building. It tells you the Eiffel Tower is so famous that almost everyone would know it straight away, just by seeing its shape.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in your own words. Does «The Eiffel Tower is a famous, easy-to-recognise building» still make sense? Yes, so iconic means very famous and easy to recognise.
explain: The second meaning is about computers and art. An icon is a small picture that stands for something, like the little picture you tap to open an app. Iconic can also describe things to do with those pictures.
fact: Iconic is an adjective, so it describes a noun: an iconic building, an iconic moment.
fact: «Iconic» means very famous and so well known that everyone recognises it.
fact: In everyday talk and the news, people call famous places, songs and outfits iconic, like a red London bus or the Sydney Opera House.
fact: «Iconic» can also mean unforgettable, as in «an iconic moment» that people still talk about years later.
fact: An icon can also be a holy picture in some churches, especially Orthodox churches.
exercise: «The Sydney Opera House is an iconic building.» What does iconic mean here? | *Very famous, so everyone recognises it | Made of wood | Sad and quiet | Very small and hard to find
exercise: Ella says the icon on her tablet opens the photo app. What is an icon here? | Ella's favourite song | A loud noise | A famous person | *A small picture that stands for something
exercise: «It was an iconic moment, one everyone in the stadium remembered.» Which word means the same as iconic here? | Wet | Tiny | Boring | *Unforgettable
test: Iconic describes a thing, so what kind of word is it? | Noun | Verb | *Adjective | Adverb
test: Which phrase is the best swap for iconic in «the iconic red bus»? | *Famous and easy to recognise | Hidden | Wet | Cheap
exam: Read: «The band played their iconic song, and the whole crowd sang along.» What does iconic mean in this sentence? | Played too quietly | *Famous and loved, so everyone knows it | Hard to hear | Written in an old book
